  "result": "```json\n{\n  \"smpl.ordering.repositories.mongodb.models.OrderDetails\": {\n    \"summary\": \"MongoDB document model class that represents order data persisted in the 'orders' collection. This class serves as a data transfer object between the MongoDB persistence layer and the domain model 'Order'. Key features include: (1) Fields: Contains an @Id annotated 'id' field for MongoDB document identification, indexed fields 'orderId', 'quoteId', and 'status' for optimized querying, along with 'orderDate' and 'events' array for order event tracking. (2) Constructors: Provides a default no-arg constructor and a conversion constructor that accepts an Order domain object and maps its properties to the MongoDB document format, converting the events list to an array. (3) Key method 'toOrder()': Converts the MongoDB document back to a domain Order object by mapping all fields and reconstructing the events list. The class uses Spring Data MongoDB annotations (@Document, @Id, @Indexed) to configure persistence behavior and query optimization.\",\n    \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/mongodb/models/OrderDetails.java\"\n  }\n}\n```",
